# The Phase 3 test map, authored as text.
#
# Reproduces what core/src/sim/testmap.cpp currently hardcodes, so the two can
# be compared byte for byte before the hardcoded one is retired.
#
#   sector 0            sector 1          sector 2
#   x 0..40 floor 0     x 40..60          x 60..80
#   west wall climbs    floor +0.5        floor 4.0 (too high: a wall)
#                       (walkable step)   east wall grapples

sector floor 0 ceil 40 tag 1
  vertex  0   0   wall
  vertex 40   0   neighbor 1
  vertex 40  40   wall
  vertex  0  40   wall climbable
end

# tag 100+N marks a mover that rises N units. The authored map decides what
# moves; Lua takes this over in Phase 4.
#
# Floor 0, flush with sector 0, and NOT the 0.5 step it used to be. A lift whose
# resting floor is above the step threshold cannot be walked onto -- correctly,
# since that is exactly what the step rule is for -- so a lift a player is meant
# to board has to be level with the ground at the bottom of its travel. The
# engine made that a design constraint rather than a bug.
sector floor 0 ceil 40 tag 101
  vertex 40   0   wall
  vertex 60   0   neighbor 2
  vertex 60  40   wall
  vertex 40  40   neighbor 0
end

sector floor 4 ceil 40 tag 3
  vertex 60   0   wall
  vertex 80   0   wall grapple
  vertex 80  40   wall
  vertex 60  40   neighbor 1
end

spawn start   10 10 2
spawn ledge   50 20 2
spawn high    70 20 6
